# Harness artefacts

Chat is ephemeral; these files are memory for **Feature** track. Direct track (feedback/bugs/finetunes) usually skips local issue folders.

## Core paths

| Path | Owner | Purpose |
|--|-|-|
| `docs/project/project.md` | planner / human | Product truth, lifecycle, delivery requirements |
| `docs/project/roadmap.md` | planner | Phases → epics; **update every Feature close** |
| `docs/project/eval-rubric.md` | planner | Global quality bar |
| `docs/project/setup.md` | human / generator | **Local verification commands**, MCPs, env vars |
| `docs/project/patterns/` | human + agents | Recurring stack/UI decisions to reuse |
| `docs/project/generator-state.md` | generator | Session handoff |
| `docs/project/issues/<id>/spec.md` | planner | Feature scope (`<id>` = Linear ID e.g. `DY-12`) |
| `docs/project/issues/<id>/rubric.md` | planner | Done-criteria; required reviewers |
| `docs/project/issues/<id>/design-direction.md` | designer | Visual contract (UI Features) |
| `docs/project/issues/<id>/assets/*-wireframe.html` | designer | **HTML** wireframe only - no generated images |
| `docs/project/feedback/<id>/` | reviewers + generator | Iteration feedback (link from Linear handoff; do not replace it) |
| `docs/project/templates/linear-handoff.md` | parent | Linear **Ready for Review** comment shape; then **In Review** status |
| `docs/adr/NNNN-*.md` | architect → human accepts | Why decisions were made |
| `CHANGELOG.md` | generator | **Required** - dated `## [x.y.z] - YYYY-MM-DD` + patch bump per cycle ([changelog](changelog.mdc)) |

Templates: `docs/project/templates/`  
Golden example: `docs/project/issues/_golden/`

**PM:** Linear = features / big adjustments. **Build/fix:** Cursor Direct track. Never dual-track - see [issue-tracking](issue-tracking.mdc).

## Work sizing (Feature track)

Agent **decides** micro-S / S / M / L / XL. Features get Linear (create/update from Cursor) + plan → generate → review. Direct work skips this.

| Size | Depth |
|--|-|
| micro-S | Linear body may serve as spec; **no code-reviewer** by default |
| S | Light spec/rubric + dated CHANGELOG + patch bump; review optional unless specialist surface |
| M | Full spec + rubric |
| L | Multiple issues; design when UI |
| XL | Phase 0 + staging |

## Design artefacts (Feature + UI)

Per [design-when](design-when.mdc) - **not** every UI Feature:

1. `design-direction.md` - palette, type, layout idea, references (prose lives here) - when designer ran
2. `assets/<slug>-wireframe.html` - **HTML** visual UI only (optional view-switch toolbar OK; no comments/legends/explanations)
3. **Dashboard UI** — `docs/design-index.json` + [dockyard-design-contract](dockyard-design-contract.mdc); §17 gaps may use issue wireframes
4. **Do not** generate mockup images / PNGs as the design contract
5. **Do not** pause for human design approval - parent continues to generator
6. When artefacts exist, AC and frontend-evaluator reference those paths; when skipped, implement from spec + patterns

## Hybrid rubric

Reviewers read **both** `eval-rubric.md` and `issues/<id>/rubric.md`. Fail if either violated. Frontend-evaluator scores against design HTML / wireframe when those artefacts exist.

## Feedback naming

One folder per Feature issue: `docs/project/feedback/<id>/`

- Reviewers: `<type>-i<iteration>.md` (e.g. `code-review-i1.md`)
- Generator only: `generator-response-i<iteration>.md`
- Never edit prior iteration files; add new files.

## ADRs

- **proposed** - not binding
- **accepted** - generator and reviewers must comply
- Link from issue spec `## Related ADRs`

## Local verification

Canonical commands in `docs/project/setup.md`.

## Patterns

After shipping a reusable approach, add a short note under `docs/project/patterns/`. Planner and generator read this folder first.
